    "summary": "Vibrant Warfield set with blistering Scarlet>Fire and an extraordinary Estimated Prophet",
    "blurb": "The second set shines with a cascading Scarlet Begonias → Fire on the Mountain transition, a soaring Estimated Prophet, and an inspired Eyes of the World. Jerry propels the band forward while Brent adds swirling texture throughout, and Phil settles into a deep groove later in the set. Soundboard recordings capture the excitement with bright tone despite typical early‑'80s tape quirks.",
    "review": "What unfolds at the Warfield on February 17, 1982 is a quintessential early‑‘80s Dead night—cohesive, adventurous, and unapologetically loud. The first set opens strong with New Minglewood Blues into Sugaree, then rolls through Bird Song and Tennessee Jed before slipping into a playful Man Smart/Woman Smarter closer. But the real fireworks ignite on the second set: Scarlet Begonias launches straight into Fire on the Mountain, where Jerry briefly pauses to savor Brent’s phrasing before delivering an incandescent lead run; the jam flows seamlessly into an expansive Estimated Prophet that many listeners describe as “transcendent,” followed by a soaring Eyes of the World that rides the band’s electric momentum all the way through drums, space, and The Wheel. The encore’s (I Can’t Get No) Satisfaction caps the night with classic crowd‑pleasing gusto. Across the various tapes, the Miller soundboard capture stands out for its bright, clear tone and relatively clean presentation of these highlights, making it the go‑to source for anyone wanting to relive this dynamic Warfield performance.",
